# This repository is PUBLIC.
#
# skills/ holds the machine-readable form of the standards in README.md, written
# for a local agent rather than for a reader. Those files cite specific private
# repositories by name as worked examples, which is what makes them useful and
# what makes them unpublishable. They stay on disk and are symlinked into
# ~/.claude/skills/ so they load in every session; they are never tracked here.
#
# If a generalized, publishable version is ever wanted, add it under a different
# path. Do not remove this entry to publish these files as they stand.
skills/

# .claude/CLAUDE.md is this repo's project instructions, and it is local for the
# same reason: it records what must not be published from here, which is not
# itself a thing to publish. Ignored rather than merely untracked, because an
# untracked file in a public repository is one careless `git add` from being
# outward-facing.
#
# That is the whole reason. This path is NOT a containment control: AGENTS.md is not
# preloaded as project instructions on Claude Code 2.1.278, so a CLAUDE.md here
# suppresses nothing.
.claude/
